    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first post office, called Lenox, opened September 29, 1826 at Cameron's Corners, with Peter Rynearson as postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lenoxville_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Settlement began in the late 18th century; Isaac Doud built a grist mill on the East Branch in 1806 to serve Lenox and neighboring townships.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lenoxville_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lenox Township formed in 1810 when Susquehanna County split from Luzerne, prompting reorganization of local boundaries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lenoxville_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community remains rural, covering 40.6 square miles of forested hills that support farming and outdoor recreation.",
